.TH URNETWORK-GUI 1 "2026-11-04" "urnetwork-client 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
urnetwork-gui \- GTK3 graphical front end for the URnetwork client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B urnetwork-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B urnetwork-gui
starts the GTK3 control panel.  It stores the account name in
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/auth
and keeps the URnetwork password in the desktop secret store (Secret Service,
normally GNOME Keyring).
.PP
Two modes are available: a local SOCKS5 proxy on
.I 127.0.0.1:9999
that needs no privileges, and a system-wide TUN VPN that installs a default
route through the tunnel.  The TUN mode requires root; the GUI launches the
engine through a root-owned helper, and a sudo askpass helper opens its own
terminal window when a password is needed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/auth
account name and network; the password is kept in the secret store
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/diagnostic.log
GUI and engine log, rotated at 10 MB
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/state.json
state written by the running VPN engine
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B URNETWORK_KEYRING
set to
.I 0
to keep the password in the auth file instead of the secret store
.TP
.B URNETWORK_PYTHON
interpreter used by the launcher script
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR urnetwork-connect (1),
.BR urnetwork-vpn (1)
